libwebrtc
---------

A build with calls (district-call's `livekit` feature) statically links
libwebrtc. On Linux it is the library District AI for Linux builds for the
LiveKit Rust SDK: LiveKit's own recipe and pinned sources for release
webrtc-89d790b of github.com/livekit/rust-sdks, with every patch LiveKit
applies, built by that repository's scripts/build-libwebrtc.sh without the H.264
and H.265 codecs or FFmpeg. The archive is webrtc-linux-x64-release.zip in
release libwebrtc-89d790b-audio-1 of
github.com/distronode-corporation/district-linux, SHA-256
2355bc8c6cdaf9613c471da944ac901bb293f346dda5e94cdbe6249a36914317, which is the
pin in scripts/fetch-libwebrtc.sh. The archive's LICENSE.md, which that script unpacks
beside the library, holds the full licence text of every component below, and a
distribution of such a build must ship it with the binary, as District AI for
Linux's packages do. This repository distributes no such build, and its default
build links none of this.

